## Your start

Several role-sessions share this repository (\<list role IDs\> + orchestrator `ORCH`).

1. Name your session: `claude -n <role-session-name>` or `/rename`.
2. Once, check `claude agents --json`: if a session with your name is already `busy` in this
   `cwd`, don't start — tell the owner.
3. **Read `coordination/roles/<ID>.md` — the only required file.** It has your zone, what's
   open, what's next, and where to go for detail.

Nothing else is required reading at start. Everything else is read on demand — see the index
below.

> Claude Code itself coordinates sessions **as processes**; this project's own rules only
> coordinate the **subject-matter** work. There are no locks, heartbeats, or nickname registries
> here — don't add them; `claude agents` already answers "who's working right now."

## Guardrails — breaking these is not easily reversible

Fill this section in with your project's actual hard constraints. Typical shape:

- Some path is **read-only** for every role except one, which touches it only under a
  one-time owner sign-off (e.g. production data, a frozen pipeline).
- `git push` — **only with the owner's direct permission**. Never force-push, `rm -rf`, or
  rewrite history.
- **Work only in your own zone.** A request outside it doesn't get done — explain whose zone it
  is, log it in `coordination/HANDOFFS.md`, offer to switch. Not sure whose zone — ask.
- Commit format: `[<ID>]` prefix + trailers **as the last paragraph, no blank line inside the
  block** (`CHARTER.md §4` has the exact gotcha and why it matters).
- Any domain-specific quality bar worth stating as a hard rule (e.g. "a fit result needs residual
  statistics, not just one number").

## Index: what to read, and when

As files grow, keep this table's byte/token estimates honest — a stale number here means a role
decides "read or skip" based on a price that stopped being true, which is worse than no estimate
at all. Whoever edits a listed file is responsible for updating its row.

`coordination/roles/<ID>.md` cold-start budget (suggest ≤1200 tokens ≈ 2400 bytes) is checked
automatically by the `SessionStart` hook this skill installs
(`.claude/hooks/check-context-budget.sh` + `budget.json`) — see `references/setup.md` in this
skill for how it's wired in. That means the number in this table can't silently go stale the way
a purely-documented budget would — the hook warns on its own when a role file grows past it.

| File | Cost | Read when |
|---|---|---|
| `coordination/roles/<ID>.md` | ≤2400 B, every role | **always, at start** |
| `coordination/CHARTER.md` | ~ | a rule is unclear or you're about to break it |
| `coordination/PROJECT.md` | ~ | need the whole role/zone table |
| `coordination/OWNERSHIP.md` | ~ | a zone dispute, or creating a new top-level directory |
| `coordination/INDEX.md` (if you generate one — see `build_index.py`) | ~ | need the open-items list from QUESTIONS/HANDOFFS without grepping |
| `coordination/QUESTIONS.md` | ~ | ⚠ **search, don't read in full** once it's grown — need the owner's decision on something |
| `coordination/HANDOFFS.md` | ~ | ⚠ **search, don't read in full** once it's grown |
| `coordination/ACTIVITY.md` | ~ | ⚠ **never in full** once it's grown — search by date/tag |

