## Path-dependent rules

If your project has commands, data formats, or domain background that only matters when a
session actually touches specific paths, don't put them in this always-loaded file — put them in
`.claude/rules/*.md` with a `paths:` frontmatter glob instead (see `references/setup.md` for the
mechanism and why it's worth using: it keeps cold start cheap for roles that never touch those
paths, while still being there automatically the moment a session does touch them).

| Rule | Fires on | What's inside |
|---|---|---|
| *(example)* `.claude/rules/pipeline-commands.md` | `src/pipeline/**` | run/test/verify commands |
